{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"surprised-overjoyful-earthworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# B — Project-only coaching move: direct the agent to Serena when source references are missed\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nA reminder at grep-time (story A) is preventive. This story adds the **corrective** half: when a review actually\nfinds that source-code references were enumerated by hand or incompletely, the agent should be coached to\nre-derive them with Serena. This is the same failure that produced three under-enumerated Scope sections in epic\n`061c` (the epic itself, S1 naming two of three patch sites, S2 naming two of four affected test files).\n\nrebar already carries project-overlay wiring for exactly this, so the story is expected to be configuration\nrather than engine work:\n\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — defines `project.*` criteria (`exec`, `facet`, `applies_at`,\n  `default_posture`, `block_threshold`) and routes them through an `activate` map into `plan_review` and/or\n  `code_review`. Existing examples: `project.portability`, `project.review-phase-boundaries`.\n- `.rebar/plan_review_moves.json` — coaching moves keyed by id with `name`, `template` (supporting `{subject}`)\n  and `applies_when` (a list of criterion ids). Existing example: `project-portability`.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd one project criterion — e.g. `project.symbol-reference-completeness` — and one matching coaching move whose\ntemplate directs re-derivation via Serena's symbol tools, with the string-literal sweep called out so the advice\nis complete rather than half-right.\n\n**Posture: advisory, not blocking.** This coaches a method, not a correctness property; a blocking posture on\n\"how did you find these references\" would be a gate on process and would fire noisily.\n\n**Where it routes** is a real decision to make from the existing machinery: incomplete file inventory is a\nplan-review concern, while \"this change missed a call site\" is a code-review concern. Route it where the\noverlay supports it, and record which.\n\n**The known unknown, stated plainly:** the moves file is named `plan_review_moves.json`, while the `activate` map\nalso supports `code_review`. Whether code-review coaching moves are overlay-driven today is unverified. If they\nare, this is pure configuration. If they are not, this story completes that wiring — and either outcome\n**dogfoods** the project-overlay feature, which is the point.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — the new `project.*` criterion + its `activate` entry.\n- `.rebar/plan_review_moves.json` — the matching move (`name` / `template` / `applies_when`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/...` — ONLY if code-review moves turn out not to be overlay-driven; then the minimum wiring to\n  make them so, kept generic (no Serena-specific or project-specific logic in shipped code).\n\n## Testing\n\n- A real `rebar review-plan` (or `review-code`) run on a ticket with a hand-written file inventory emits the new\n  coaching move; the run output is attached to this ticket as evidence.\n- The criterion does not fire on a ticket whose inventory is already symbol-derived (contrast case).\n- The shipped default criteria set is unchanged for other clients.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a project-only criterion + coaching move exists whose move text directs re-deriving source references with\n      Serena's symbol tools, including the string-literal (`monkeypatch.setattr`/`getattr`) sweep the LSP cannot do\n- [ ] a REAL `rebar review-plan`/`review-code` run emits the move, with the output attached as a comment on this\n      ticket (not a unit-test-only demonstration)\n- [ ] the criterion is advisory (`default_posture`), never blocking\n- [ ] the criterion rides the `.rebar/` overlay only: `grep -rn '<criterion-id>' src/rebar/` is empty, proving\n      the shipped default criteria set is unchanged for other rebar clients\n- [ ] it is recorded on the ticket whether code-review coaching moves were already overlay-driven, and if wiring\n      was added, that wiring contains no project-specific or Serena-specific logic","id":"84c7-ad6c-be99-4c30","parent_id":"9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"B — Project-only coaching move directing Serena when source references are missed"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785368701947686001,"uuid":"f43e493b-f118-4c6d-a5b2-6a55c91d6239"}